patch.description:
Purely additive: mount the five safe connector intents beside the four connector tools already registered. registerAgentConnectorTools skips any name already taken (it knows connectorServerToolNames), so mounting both is safe and the five ceremony tools are untouched. Exact patch: (1) after the existing `import { registerConnectorServerTools } from "./connectors/mcp/server-tools.js";` line add `import { registerAgentConnectorTools } from "./connectors/agents/mcp-intents.js";` and `import type { AgentConnectorDependencies } from "./connectors/agents/intents.js";`. (2) in `CeremonyMcpOptions`, after the `connectors?: ConnectorToolDependencies;` field add:

  /**
   * Safe connector intents (list, inspect, operations, reconnect,
   * disconnect), when this deployment offers them. Names already registered
   * are skipped, so this only ever adds.
   */
  connectorIntents?: AgentConnectorDependencies;

(3) in `build(context)`, immediately after the existing block

    if (options.connectors)
      registerConnectorServerTools(server, options.connectors, {
        actor: () => actor,
        ...(options.onerror ? { onerror: options.onerror } : {}),
      });

add

    if (options.connectorIntents)
      registerAgentConnectorTools(server, options.connectorIntents, {
        actor: () => actor,
        ...(options.onerror ? { onerror: options.onerror } : {}),
      });

No other line changes. Leaving `connectorIntents` unset changes nothing.

Add, after `export * from "./connectors.js";`:
export * from "./connector-directory.js";
export * from "./connector-drawer.js";
export * from "./connector-connection.js";
export { ConnectorImport, DefinitionReviewPanel, IssueList, DimensionTable } from "./connector-review.js";
Note: connector-directory.tsx and connector-connection.tsx both export `dimensionLabels`/`evidencePresentation` only from the directory module, so a flat re-export is collision-free. If the review surface should stay out of the package entry (bundle), export only the first three lines.
